Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: lengthen the PPE UDP bind age

PPE_BIND_AGE0_DELTA_UDP is how long a bound UDP flow is kept in the PPE
table before it falls back to the unbound state. The hardcoded 60 is
short for P2P/PCDN workloads whose flows idle for a few seconds between
bursts: the entry is evicted, the next packet has to be re-bound and
meanwhile the flow is served by the software path.

Raise it to 180 so low-rate UDP flows stay offloaded.

Signed-off-by: zhoufl <zhoufl@localhost>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -112,7 +112,7 @@
 			      PPE_BIND_AGE0_DELTA_NON_L4 |
 			      PPE_BIND_AGE0_DELTA_UDP,
 			      FIELD_PREP(PPE_BIND_AGE0_DELTA_NON_L4, 60) |
-			      FIELD_PREP(PPE_BIND_AGE0_DELTA_UDP, 60));
+			      FIELD_PREP(PPE_BIND_AGE0_DELTA_UDP, 180));
 		airoha_fe_rmw(eth, REG_PPE_BND_AGE1(i),
 			      PPE_BIND_AGE1_DELTA_TCP_FIN |
 			      PPE_BIND_AGE1_DELTA_TCP,
